 sel="Generals, colonels and selected civilian officials and business leaders",
 d="Brazilian generals created the school in 1949 after General Salvador César Obino visited the US National War College in 1948; officers who had trained with Americans during the Second World War modelled it on that college. It taught a 'national security doctrine' that treated the Cold War as an internal revolutionary war. A 2010 study in the journal História describes the doctrine as the theoretical frame of the military government that took power in 1964 and ruled until 1985, and Portuguese Wikipedia files the school among organisations tied to that dictatorship.",
