 sel="Foreigners aged 25 to 35 from politics, business, media and civil society, often by referral; trips paid in full",
 d="Since 2011 the Russian government has paid for young foreign 'representatives of social and political circles' to tour Russia and meet officials. In 2013 the FBI investigated whether the head of the agency's Washington office used the trips, which had brought about 130 young Americans to Russia, to cultivate intelligence assets; Moscow denied it. The Dossier Center reported in 2021 that the agency employs FSB and SVR officers. iStories reported in 2025 that the agency planned a record 357.3 million rubles for the programme to host 1,600 people, and quoted the organisers' expectation that participants would reach high posts at home and stay loyal to the Kremlin. The EU sanctioned the agency in 2022.",
